WEBVTT

00:00.640 --> 00:02.730
Good morning, Nishimura-san!

00:03.150 --> 00:05.010
Good morning, Takada-kun.

00:05.010 --> 00:06.920
You're as awesome as ever today!

00:06.920 --> 00:08.730
Y-You think?

00:15.210 --> 00:17.250
So, Nishimura-san...

00:17.770 --> 00:19.810
What's up with you and Takada-kun?

00:19.810 --> 00:20.800
Huh?

00:20.800 --> 00:23.620
Are you two going out after all?

00:23.620 --> 00:27.130
I-It's nothing like that.

00:27.130 --> 00:29.970
But you're always together.

00:30.610 --> 00:36.060
Takada-kun and I, um... wouldn't 
be a good match for each other.

00:36.330 --> 00:39.010
Hmm? In other words...

00:39.280 --> 00:44.280
You're bored of Takada-kun 
because he's not good enough?

00:45.750 --> 00:46.630
What?!

00:52.400 --> 00:54.400
Th-That's not it.

00:54.400 --> 00:58.120
When I said we weren't 
a good match, I meant...

00:58.120 --> 00:59.990
Hey, hey! Did you hear?

01:00.250 --> 01:04.880
She said playing with Takada-kun is no fun.

01:05.110 --> 01:06.870
N-No...

01:08.320 --> 01:09.750
Is that so?

01:10.060 --> 01:13.040
Guess I haven't been trying hard enough...

01:13.040 --> 01:15.760
for a human hanging out
 with the Grim Reaper...

01:16.460 --> 01:17.610
<i>This isn't right.</i>

01:17.610 --> 01:20.770
<i>I was expecting a different 
kind of disappointment...</i>

01:21.040 --> 01:24.210
I'll need to do my best not to bore you...

01:24.210 --> 01:25.880
I-It's okay!

01:26.230 --> 01:28.570
I have lots of fun!

01:28.970 --> 01:30.350
Really.

01:30.350 --> 01:35.290
Just being with you,
I have as much fun as you do.

01:35.290 --> 01:37.790
That can't be true, Nishimura-san!

01:38.790 --> 01:40.290
There's no way!

01:40.290 --> 01:46.510
When you have fun,
I have an even way, way better time!

01:46.510 --> 01:47.590
What?!

01:47.590 --> 01:53.350
So I need to make sure you're having
 even <i>more</i> fun! That you're even happier!

01:53.350 --> 01:56.730
But I'm totally happy with things as they are.

01:56.730 --> 01:58.370
You can be honest with me!

01:58.370 --> 02:00.220
I'm just trying to be a good match for you!

02:00.450 --> 02:02.800
Y-You don't need to worry about that...

02:02.800 --> 02:08.220
I'll do whatever I can
to make you super-duper happy!

02:08.220 --> 02:11.660
L-Like I said, I'm fine with things now...

02:12.690 --> 02:15.320
What are you even trying 
to accomplish with all this?

03:42.910 --> 03:46.990
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

03:47.530 --> 03:52.540
<i>Episode 7 "Field Trips and the Magic of Marinated Eggs"</i>

03:48.410 --> 03:50.630
Nishimura-san, Nishimura-san!

03:50.630 --> 03:53.500
Let's play out on the field during recess!

03:54.110 --> 03:56.530
S-Sorry, Takada-kun.

03:56.530 --> 03:59.480
I'm busy right now, so maybe later!

03:59.940 --> 04:01.770
I'll help you, Akane-chan.

04:01.770 --> 04:04.020
Ah, thanks.

04:04.020 --> 04:05.690
Where are we taking these?

04:05.690 --> 04:07.140
The teachers' lounge.

04:08.400 --> 04:10.640
Those two sure are close.

04:14.350 --> 04:16.860
Teachers' Lounge

04:19.260 --> 04:21.060
Thanks, you two.

04:21.060 --> 04:23.770
Could you also take those 
back to the classroom?

04:25.490 --> 04:27.830
<b>Field Trip Guide</b>

04:25.490 --> 04:27.830
<b>Field Trip Guide</b>

04:28.800 --> 04:33.070
<i>My first field trip with Takada-kun...</i>

04:31.040 --> 04:35.170
<b>Field Trip Guide</b>

04:33.070 --> 04:34.480
<i>I can't wait.</i>

04:36.010 --> 04:37.860
A field trip!

04:37.080 --> 04:40.840
<b>Field Trip</b>

04:37.860 --> 04:40.840
All right, let's decide the bus seating chart.

04:41.420 --> 04:43.460
I'll sit with Nishimura-san!

04:43.460 --> 04:44.650
Sensei!

04:45.640 --> 04:53.160
For our bus seats, I think we should sit 
with people we don't usually talk to!

04:53.160 --> 04:54.570
I like that idea.

04:54.930 --> 04:57.080
Huh? Why do we have to do that?

04:57.080 --> 04:59.360
Stop whining! It's just for the bus ride.

04:59.360 --> 05:00.690
Sounds interesting!

05:01.560 --> 05:05.070
<i>People we don't usually talk to...</i>

05:05.410 --> 05:09.620
Okay, talk it out among yourselves
and tell me when you've decided.

05:09.620 --> 05:10.920
Okay!

05:10.260 --> 05:13.720
Takada-kun, you're always 
talking with Nishimura-san.

05:13.720 --> 05:16.070
Why not sit with someone else?

05:16.070 --> 05:18.460
What?! No way!

05:18.860 --> 05:20.880
<i>I-I see.</i>

05:20.880 --> 05:21.960
<i>That makes sense.</i>

05:23.070 --> 05:24.590
<i>What do I do?</i>

05:24.590 --> 05:27.730
<i>I'm sure no one wants to sit next to me...</i>

05:29.060 --> 05:31.020
Akane-chan, Akane-chan!

05:32.760 --> 05:34.090
Umi-chan?

05:35.000 --> 05:39.110
We haven't gotten much of a chance
 to talk at school yet,

05:39.110 --> 05:41.940
so I think it's fine if we sit together!

05:42.830 --> 05:45.110
Y-You think so?

05:45.620 --> 05:47.780
We can trade snacks and stuff!

05:47.780 --> 05:48.530
Yeah!

05:49.440 --> 05:51.120
Who should take the window seat?

05:51.120 --> 05:53.470
I-I don't mind either way.

05:57.040 --> 05:57.760
Ah...

05:58.940 --> 06:02.240
I'll be fine, Takada-kun.

06:02.590 --> 06:04.790
So you should find someone else to...

06:04.790 --> 06:06.620
F-Fine by me!

06:06.620 --> 06:08.540
Totally fine by me!

06:08.540 --> 06:12.560
I'll sit with someone I've never talked to!

06:14.000 --> 06:15.250
<i>Huh?</i>

06:16.020 --> 06:18.980
Takada, you talk with everyone.

06:19.720 --> 06:21.770
Wanna sit with me, then?

06:22.980 --> 06:25.520
I-Is he sulking?

06:25.780 --> 06:29.150
<b>Bus driver</b>

06:25.780 --> 06:29.150
<b>Seto & Kimoto</b>

06:25.780 --> 06:29.150
<b>Kasahara & Takada</b>

06:25.780 --> 06:29.150
<b>Kobayashi & Hino</b>

06:25.780 --> 06:29.150
<b>Sensei</b>

06:25.780 --> 06:29.150
<b>Tanaka</b>

06:25.780 --> 06:29.150
<b>Mori</b>

06:25.780 --> 06:29.150
<b>Miyazaki</b>

06:29.480 --> 06:33.290
<i>Takada's sitting next to Kasahara-san?</i>

06:33.880 --> 06:35.710
Nishimura-san.

06:35.710 --> 06:38.400
About our class rep duties
on the field trip...

06:38.590 --> 06:43.090
If anyone ends up feeling sick, 
you can look after them.

06:43.090 --> 06:43.810
What?

06:44.470 --> 06:46.970
I'll be taking roll call and stuff.

06:46.970 --> 06:50.160
Since you're so quiet, Nishimura-san.

06:50.160 --> 06:51.840
O-Okay...

06:52.070 --> 06:53.850
All right, that's all I had to say.

06:53.850 --> 06:55.170
Thanks a ton!

06:59.270 --> 07:01.690
Kasahara-san's so mean!

07:01.690 --> 07:04.730
She's pushing all the annoying work on you.

07:05.290 --> 07:08.330
It's fine. I don't mind.

07:09.270 --> 07:10.430
What?!

07:10.430 --> 07:11.890
Then how about almond tofu?

07:11.890 --> 07:13.710
Does it count as a snack?

07:13.710 --> 07:16.990
It's apparently a palate 
cleanser, not a snack.

07:16.990 --> 07:18.280
Huh...

07:19.320 --> 07:23.350
<i>For some reason, Takada-kun 
feels really far away today.</i>

07:23.960 --> 07:28.010
<i>My first field trip with Takada-kun...</i>

07:29.380 --> 07:32.890
<b>Kasahara & Takada</b>

07:29.630 --> 07:31.790
<i>I was so excited about it.</i>

07:35.450 --> 07:38.110
Akane, can you go get the toothpicks?

07:38.110 --> 07:38.850
Yeah.

07:42.270 --> 07:43.280
Here.

07:43.280 --> 07:44.340
Thanks.

07:45.580 --> 07:49.070
Why do you always put marinated 
eggs in my lunch box?

07:49.610 --> 07:51.340
And so many, at that.

07:51.850 --> 07:54.320
Mmm, well...

07:55.110 --> 07:57.340
It's my little magic spell.

07:58.220 --> 07:59.440
Hmm?

08:00.160 --> 08:02.300
Okay, all done.

08:04.990 --> 08:08.050
Okay, Dad, I'm leaving!

08:08.280 --> 08:09.900
Remember everything?

08:09.900 --> 08:11.260
I'm good.

08:11.260 --> 08:12.920
Thanks for my lunch.

08:13.240 --> 08:14.780
You have fun today.

08:18.050 --> 08:19.260
What's the matter?

08:19.570 --> 08:20.670
Nothing.

08:21.490 --> 08:22.760
I'm off!

08:22.760 --> 08:24.220
Have a good trip.

08:29.690 --> 08:32.900
<b>That-There Elementary School
Entrance Ceremony</b>

08:31.370 --> 08:32.910
Look, Akane.

08:33.280 --> 08:36.150
There're lots of kids your age over there!

08:37.160 --> 08:39.780
<i><i>Akane's been shy since she was little</i></i>

08:40.410 --> 08:43.170
<i><i>and seemingly had a hard time making friends.</i></i>

08:45.970 --> 08:48.160
<i><i>No matter how much you love them,</i></i>

08:48.830 --> 08:53.830
<i><i>parents can't go to school
and make friends for their children.</i></i>

08:55.100 --> 08:58.940
<i><i>So, as her father, 
the least I can do is help Akane to...</i></i>

09:09.310 --> 09:11.480
Sensei, bad news!

09:11.480 --> 09:14.860
Takada's super carsick!

09:14.860 --> 09:16.100
What?!

09:16.340 --> 09:18.510
G-Gonna hurl...

09:18.510 --> 09:19.240
Anyone!

09:19.240 --> 09:20.740
I need a bag here!

09:21.420 --> 09:22.950
<i>Ah, sheesh!</i>

09:22.950 --> 09:25.780
<i>Just when I got to sit next to him!</i>

09:26.110 --> 09:27.460
<i>Takada-kun...</i>

09:27.840 --> 09:30.460
Where did I put my travel sickness medicine?

09:33.160 --> 09:35.390
You all right there, Takada?

09:35.390 --> 09:37.070
I can't do it...

09:37.070 --> 09:40.850
You all go on without me...

09:40.850 --> 09:43.630
You know we can't do that.

09:43.630 --> 09:46.920
One of the class reps will stay behind,
so catch up with us later.

09:47.820 --> 09:49.940
I-In that case, I'll...

09:49.940 --> 09:52.970
Huh? I thought that was my job.

09:52.970 --> 09:54.990
What? You got a problem?

09:54.990 --> 09:56.440
You moron.

09:57.150 --> 10:01.460
Leave the annoying work like that
to the Grim Reaper.

10:01.460 --> 10:02.620
What?!

10:02.620 --> 10:07.870
You've gotta take roll call,
so just leave the Grim Reaper here!

10:09.100 --> 10:10.550
<i>Put a sock in it, baldy!</i>

10:10.860 --> 10:13.980
<i>Now's not the time for your 
Grim Reaper nonsense!</i>

10:13.980 --> 10:17.170
Wh-What gives?
I'm trying to help you out here.

10:17.170 --> 10:19.480
<i>I want to be with Takada-kun!</i>

10:19.480 --> 10:20.540
<i>Get a clue!</i>

10:20.920 --> 10:23.270
<i>But I can't say that out loud!</i>

10:23.270 --> 10:25.300
C'mon, Kasahara-san.

10:25.300 --> 10:26.580
Off we go.

10:27.600 --> 10:29.760
Wh-What's with her?

10:30.320 --> 10:33.800
Kitagawa, could it be that they hate you?

10:33.800 --> 10:34.980
Huh?!

10:34.980 --> 10:38.540
Hold on, don't call your 
classmate the Grim Reaper!

10:41.410 --> 10:45.230
We'll be about a fifteen-minute
 walk from here,

10:45.230 --> 10:48.120
so if anything happens,
use this money to call me.

10:48.120 --> 10:51.750
Oh, that's okay, I have a phone.

10:51.750 --> 10:52.870
Is that right?

10:52.870 --> 10:56.790
Well, hold on to this anyway
just in case something happens.

10:58.720 --> 10:59.600
Okay.

11:00.220 --> 11:01.710
Take care of Takada.

11:04.210 --> 11:06.080
Let's get going, Umi!

11:06.080 --> 11:08.590
Y-Yeah, let's!

11:16.820 --> 11:21.660
<i>Thanks to Kitagawa-kun,
I'm alone with Takada-kun.</i>

11:22.580 --> 11:25.980
<i>I mean, we play together all the time.</i>

11:27.420 --> 11:31.370
<i>But this feels a little different.</i>

11:53.320 --> 11:56.720
T-Takada-kun, are you all right?

12:05.780 --> 12:07.730
I'm sorry, Kasahara-san!

12:07.730 --> 12:09.070
Wait, huh?

12:09.600 --> 12:11.260
Nishimura-san?

12:11.260 --> 12:12.080
Yeah.

12:13.360 --> 12:17.330
Oh, no wonder I feel better!

12:19.690 --> 12:21.540
Th-That can't be...

12:21.540 --> 12:24.660
It's true! I feel better for some reason!

12:24.660 --> 12:26.860
It's gotta be your curse powers!

12:27.830 --> 12:31.960
If you're feeling better, then I'm glad.

12:32.420 --> 12:33.940
Where's everyone else?

12:33.940 --> 12:35.490
They went on ahead.

12:35.490 --> 12:39.340
I was looking after you as class rep.

12:39.340 --> 12:40.490
Makes sense.

12:40.780 --> 12:42.670
Thanks, Nishimura-san.

12:44.590 --> 12:46.500
Sorry about all this.

12:46.500 --> 12:48.500
Huh? For what?

12:48.750 --> 12:53.190
This was your chance to get 
to know Adachi-san better,

12:53.190 --> 12:55.950
and I ended up getting in the way...

12:56.220 --> 13:02.540
The truth is, I was holding back on 
getting to know <i>you</i> even more...

13:04.460 --> 13:08.130
We still haven't gotten much
 of a chance to talk yet!

13:09.440 --> 13:13.460
<i>Takada-kun was thinking of me.</i>

13:13.940 --> 13:19.090
<i>That's why he was doing his best to back off.</i>

13:19.860 --> 13:22.480
<i>He didn't have to do any of that.</i>

13:22.480 --> 13:25.980
<i>He doesn't need to be so considerate of me...</i>

13:27.120 --> 13:29.220
What's wrong, Nishimura-san?

13:29.220 --> 13:32.090
O-Oh, it's nothing.

13:32.090 --> 13:33.580
Oh, really?

13:35.250 --> 13:41.180
<i>If only I could find one fun thing
 to do with Takada-kun...</i>

13:43.370 --> 13:45.040
Hey, Takada-kun.

13:45.890 --> 13:46.750
What is it?

13:47.420 --> 13:51.740
D-Do you want to... take a detour?

13:56.830 --> 14:02.640
I-I was looking forward to coming 
on this field trip with you,

14:02.640 --> 14:03.750
so...

14:04.360 --> 14:06.980
I want you to feel better, or, well...

14:07.920 --> 14:09.410
A detour?!

14:16.410 --> 14:18.880
This is so exciting, Nishimura-san!

14:18.880 --> 14:21.060
It feels like we're being naughty!

14:21.060 --> 14:24.410
O-Only for a little bit! Really!

14:24.420 --> 14:27.420
<b>Pharmacy</b>

14:30.430 --> 14:32.930
<b>Persimmon Parfait  1,500 yen</b>

14:30.430 --> 14:32.930
<b>Melon Parfait  1,800 yen</b>

14:47.180 --> 14:49.790
<i>There was nothing to be worried about.</i>

14:51.140 --> 14:56.150
<i>Takada-kun is always thoughtful 
about the people around him.</i>

14:56.660 --> 14:59.420
<b>Mystic Stones 5,000 yen</b>

14:56.660 --> 14:59.420
<b>Filled with cosmic power!!</b>

15:09.720 --> 15:12.870
<i>It really does feel like we're being naughty.</i>

15:13.650 --> 15:15.090
<i>Just the two of us.</i>

15:15.830 --> 15:16.860
What?

15:16.860 --> 15:19.950
You used all the money I gave you?

15:20.510 --> 15:21.670
On <i>snacks</i>?

15:21.670 --> 15:23.880
W-We're sorry.

15:27.320 --> 15:29.820
Don't tell any of the other kids.

15:30.220 --> 15:33.340
Well, I'm glad you're 
feeling better, Takada.

15:33.340 --> 15:34.830
Sensei!

15:35.630 --> 15:39.080
<i>Our field trip has just begun!</i>

15:39.960 --> 15:44.960
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

15:47.980 --> 15:49.710
<b>Space Museum</b>

15:49.700 --> 15:52.170
We're finally here!

15:52.170 --> 15:53.660
Hey!

15:54.350 --> 15:55.860
Hino-kun!

15:55.860 --> 15:57.860
Are you feeling better, Takada-kun?

15:57.860 --> 16:01.660
You were taking so long, I thought 
you might have gone on a detour.

16:01.660 --> 16:02.790
Eh?!

16:02.790 --> 16:06.070
N-No, we came straight here!

16:06.070 --> 16:07.610
Isn't that right, Nishimura-san?

16:07.610 --> 16:08.810
Y-Yeah.

16:09.190 --> 16:11.690
It's good to be reunited.

16:11.690 --> 16:13.580
Let's tour the place together, Akane-chan.

16:13.580 --> 16:15.240
Th-Thanks.

16:16.630 --> 16:18.870
I'm sorry, Adachi-san.

16:19.180 --> 16:21.450
Huh? Wh-What for?

16:21.720 --> 16:26.460
I ended up hogging Nishimura-san 
all to myself again.

16:26.890 --> 16:32.040
I was trying not to get in the 
way of you two making friends.

16:32.040 --> 16:33.190
What?

16:33.190 --> 16:35.480
You don't need to worry about that!

16:35.750 --> 16:39.460
We're perfectly good friends already.

16:40.260 --> 16:41.970
What?! Really?!

16:42.250 --> 16:43.950
Isn't that right, Akane-chan?

16:43.950 --> 16:45.600
Y-Yeah!

16:47.740 --> 16:49.970
I'm so glad!

16:49.970 --> 16:51.150
Takada, Takada!

16:51.150 --> 16:53.120
There's something real awesome over there!

16:53.580 --> 16:55.970
It's a space probe!

16:55.970 --> 16:58.490
Whoa! It's bigger than I thought!

16:58.490 --> 17:00.460
Should we write our report on this?

17:02.480 --> 17:05.300
You're into space stuff, Nishimura-san?

17:05.300 --> 17:07.100
I-Is that weird?

17:07.100 --> 17:08.820
That's not weird at all.

17:09.080 --> 17:11.080
You look like you're having loads of fun.

17:11.080 --> 17:12.870
I think that's great!

17:13.230 --> 17:20.610
Y-You see, when I was little, 
my dad took me to the planetarium here.

17:20.980 --> 17:23.960
So I got a little overexcited.

17:23.960 --> 17:27.110
Huh, they have a planetarium here?

17:28.140 --> 17:32.950
<i>The truth is that it's because I'm 
here with Takada-kun and the others.</i>

17:32.950 --> 17:36.050
You think we can eat astronaut food here?

17:36.050 --> 17:37.690
Are you hungry?

17:40.380 --> 17:44.710
Your lunch box is full of boiled eggs!

17:44.710 --> 17:48.130
They're not just boiled, they're marinated.

17:48.130 --> 17:49.420
Marinated?!

17:49.420 --> 17:50.580
What is this, ramen?

17:50.910 --> 17:54.840
My lunch boxes always have 
marinated eggs in them.

17:55.060 --> 17:56.350
Is that weird?

17:56.350 --> 18:01.110
It's not strange, but marinated eggs 
in a lunch box is quite a surprise.

18:01.110 --> 18:02.290
What is this, ramen?

18:05.440 --> 18:08.390
So it's unusual...

18:08.780 --> 18:11.200
Those marinated eggs look good!

18:11.200 --> 18:13.290
Wanna trade sides with me?

18:13.290 --> 18:14.110
What?

18:15.230 --> 18:16.980
Y-Yeah!

18:17.250 --> 18:19.240
Then a wiener from me!

18:19.240 --> 18:20.770
Fries from me!

18:20.770 --> 18:22.480
And from me...

18:23.320 --> 18:24.760
<i>Wow!</i>

18:25.470 --> 18:30.950
<i>Right now, I'm having a good time talking 
about lunches with my friends!</i>

18:31.620 --> 18:36.240
<i>I've never traded my sides 
with friends before...</i>

18:36.800 --> 18:39.260
It's steeped with flavor! How delicious!

18:39.260 --> 18:41.210
Tastes like ramen!

18:41.210 --> 18:44.020
Akane-chan, your marinated 
eggs are a big hit!

18:44.020 --> 18:47.310
And you had plenty to share with everyone!

18:47.310 --> 18:50.890
Yeah, since my dad packed so many.

18:51.530 --> 18:52.470
Huh?

18:52.470 --> 18:55.070
<i>Akane, can you go get the toothpicks?</i>

18:56.280 --> 18:59.690
<i>Why do you always put marinated 
eggs in my lunch box?</i>

18:59.690 --> 19:01.440
<i>And so many, at that.</i>

19:02.180 --> 19:04.360
<i>It's my little magic spell.</i>

19:05.720 --> 19:07.080
<i>A magic spell...</i>

19:08.510 --> 19:14.050
<i>Wait, was Dad trying to make it easier 
for me to start a conversation?</i>

19:14.470 --> 19:16.590
What's wrong, Nishimura-san?

19:16.590 --> 19:17.550
Huh?!

19:17.550 --> 19:19.790
I-I-It's nothing, really!

19:19.790 --> 19:22.810
Really? Your face is red.

19:22.810 --> 19:24.070
<i>Takada-kun!</i>

19:24.070 --> 19:26.400
<i>That's because of you!</i>

19:27.760 --> 19:29.520
H-Hey, everyone.

19:30.860 --> 19:32.560
Do you mind?

19:48.310 --> 19:50.930
<i>Akane's been shy since she was little</i>

19:51.280 --> 19:54.270
<i>and I thought she found 
it hard to make friends.</i>

19:56.010 --> 19:57.080
<i>My magic spell...</i>

19:58.300 --> 20:02.970
<i>"May Akane make some good friends."</i>

20:04.920 --> 20:10.260
<i>The marinated eggs you made were 
a big hit with my friends.</i>

20:19.990 --> 20:21.310
Akane...

20:26.430 --> 20:29.360
Hey, hurry up and get in here.

20:29.830 --> 20:32.320
We can't get started without everyone.

20:32.840 --> 20:35.630
Ah, right. Sorry about that.

20:48.410 --> 20:50.820
It's so pretty, Nishimura-san!

20:51.130 --> 20:51.790
Yeah!

20:58.060 --> 21:01.070
Hey, Umi, isn't that Planet 
Tank Top over there?

21:01.070 --> 21:03.200
Let's see if we can find Scorpius!

21:03.200 --> 21:03.960
Yeah!

21:03.960 --> 21:04.780
Wait, isn't that it?

21:04.780 --> 21:05.790
Huh? Where? Where?!

21:15.290 --> 21:17.170
To commemorate your visit
<b>Souvenir Voucher</b>
- Redeem with a museum shop employee.
- Limit one per visitor.

21:22.970 --> 21:23.990
Space Rice Ball

21:22.970 --> 21:26.550
Space Curry

21:22.970 --> 21:26.550
Space Ice Cream

21:33.020 --> 21:34.690
Akane

21:33.020 --> 21:34.690
I'm bringing back a souvenir for you.

21:44.920 --> 21:46.260
<i>Dad...</i>

21:47.470 --> 21:49.670
<i>I think I'll be okay now.</i>

21:52.350 --> 21:54.080
<i>Today's field trip...</i>

21:55.360 --> 21:57.500
<i>was lots of fun!</i>

23:34.970 --> 23:39.970
<b>Next time...</b>

23:34.970 --> 23:39.970
<b>Yukata, Jungle Gyms, and Orthopedic Casts</b>
